Repository Pushing Guidelines
==============================
Refer to this guide when determining which files to push to which repository.

1. Backend Repository (dev organizational repo):
   * Link: https://github.com/cloudshiftsolutions-dev/Backend---NFC-QR-code-Management
   * Rule: Only update and push if files in the `backend` folder are updated.

2. Frontend Repository (dev organizational repo):
   * Link: https://github.com/cloudshiftsolutions-dev/Frontend---NFC-QR-code-Management
   * Rule: Push frontend-updates.

3. Web Frontend Repository (dev organizational repo):
   * Link: https://github.com/cloudshiftsolutions-dev/Web-Frontend---NFC-QR-code-Management
   * Rule: Push to dev's `web-frontend` repo.

4. Personal ID Repository (NFC-QR-CODE):
   * Link: https://github.com/divyanscloudshiftsolutions/NFC-QR-code
   * Rule: Push `frontend` only.

5. EAS / EIS Updates:
   * Rule: Update the respective location in the repo (run EAS builds/updates in `frontend/frontend` folder).

If there is any confusion in pushing updated files to Git, reference this file to verify which file goes to which repository.
